    dtps: "1. Advanced HIV with severe immunosuppression requiring urgent ART initiation. 2. High risk of OIs (PCP, TB, Cryptococcus) requiring prophylaxis. 3. Public health: transmission risk requiring prevention counselling.",
    monitoring: "CD4 count at baseline (not needed to start ART). Viral load at 6 months, then annually. Creatinine at baseline, 3 months (tenofovir renal safety). Hb (AZT effect). Weight and nutritional status. Adherence at every visit. Screen for TB symptoms at every visit.",
