    followUp: "HIV clinic in 2 weeks. Viral load in 6 months (target <50 copies/mL). CD4 monitoring 6-monthly until >200. Annual cervical cancer screening (women). Annual STI screening. Long-term: CV risk, bone density (tenofovir), renal function monitoring.",
    pearls: "Kenya uses the \"Test and Treat\" strategy — start ART on the same day as diagnosis regardless of CD4 count. Dolutegravir is the preferred third agent in Kenya (TLD regimen) — potent, well-tolerated, high barrier to resistance. Tenofovir can cause renal impairment — monitor creatinine. CTX prophylaxis is life-saving at CD4 <200 (prevents PCP, toxoplasmosis, bacterial infections). U=U (Undetectable = Untransmittable) is scientifically proven when viral load <200 copies/mL.",
